Hello NetHack Gurus,

I have just fetched and compiled NetHack 3.1.  My life is now complete.
However, I have a number of comments and questions, mainly about the new
X11 interface.

1. How do you specify which window interface to use dynamically?  I have
   to resort to editing the binary to switch between "tty" and "X11".

2. Typeahead is ignored when the X11 popup is used.  This is most
   noticeable when opening doors ("ol") and invoking extended commands
   ("#l") and kicking ("^Dj").  It is annoying when you need to repeat an
   action many times that asks for confirmation.

3. The visibility rules seem to have some strange bugs.  I often see
   things far away across the level that are only reachable through twisty
   passages.  There is no straight line of sight to the things I am being
   shown.

4. The pop-up inventory is nice.  Is there a way to leave it up while you
   do other things?  Ideally it would be updated while left visible.  An
   "inventory tool" that allowed you to drop, put on, or take off things
   would be really cool.  A similar sort of "object tool" for the things
   on the ground in the current location would be nice too.

5. The X11 message window flashes for some messages and not for others.
   This is disconcerting.

6. How do you set the number of lines remembered in the message window?
   I'd like it to remember the last 1000.

7. The popup dialog boxes are *very slow*.  Is it possible to get the
   interface to just pop up one box and change the text inside it instead?
   I tried setting "NetHack*slow: True" in NetHack.ad, but it didn't have
   any effect.  I followed the instructions and put NetHack.ad in
   nethackdir and added this line to nethack:

     XAPPLRESDIR="$HACKDIR"; export XAPPLRESDIR

   (Yes, I restarted nethack after making the changes!)

8. The popup dialog box's insistence on appearing underneath the X cursor
   makes it hard to read the contents of the box.  Short object names
   often are entirely obscured by the cursor.

9. The message window should automatically jump to the bottom of the text
   when a new message gets added to the end.

10. The popup that lets you type text expands *very slowly* when you type
    more text than will fit.  This is easily seen when wishing for the
    neat stuff.


While I'm at it, some long standing requests ...

* Auto-pickup of just money.

* Automatic opening attempt of doors when it is attempted to move through
  one.

Anyway, I hope this message inspires someone to fix things.

